-- S0-2 (review round of `ffi-lower-and-link`): a NULLARY user extern is
-- rejected.  A signature with no arrow has nowhere to write the required `FFI`
-- label -- an effect row lives on an arrow's RESULT -- so `ffiRowHasFFITy`
-- answers `None` here, which the label rule USED to treat as "not applicable,
-- pass".  While it did, the #2074 emitter still lowered the name as a foreign
-- call (`emitVar`'s `isFfiExtern` arm -> `emitFfiEtaClosure`), so this program
-- printed an eta CLOSURE POINTER where an `Int` was expected, at exit 0.  Before
-- that lowering it died loudly with `unbound variable`, so the pass here is what
-- made a loud failure silent ([W-QUIETER]).
--
-- 🚨 Read together with `ffi_stamp_narrow_accept.mdk`: the difference is only
-- whether an ARROW exists, so a fix that rejected every extern would show green
-- here and red there.  #2106 -- how a nullary extern WOULD spell a label -- is a
-- separate, still-open design question; this cell pins only the refusal.
extern gNullary : Int

main : <IO> Unit
main = println (gNullary + 1)
